# Drop.ai Web DAW User Guide

This document provides user instructions for the web DAW features and AI functionality.

## 🎵 Metronome Usage

### Basic Controls
- **Enable Metronome**: Check the checkbox at the top
- **Set BPM**: Enter desired speed (30-300 BPM)
- **Play**: Click play button → metronome clicks start
- **Stop**: Click stop button → metronome immediately stops

### Real-time Control
- Change BPM and metronome state while playing
- Uncheck metronome checkbox for instant mute
- BPM changes reflect in real-time

## ▶️ Play/Stop Control

### Transport Buttons
- **Play Button**: Click to start playback with metronome
- **Stop Button**: Click to stop all playback, reset position

### Position Display
- **Bar:Beat**: Current playback position (e.g., 1:1, 2:3)
- **Seconds**: Precise time display (e.g., 0.00s, 2.45s)

## 📏 Timeline Usage

### Ruler Display
- **Bar Division**: Thick vertical lines mark bar start points
- **Beat Division**: Thin vertical lines mark beat divisions
- **Bar Numbers**: Numbers displayed at each bar start

### Playhead
- **During Playback**: Red vertical line moves right showing current position
- **When Stopped**: Fixed at last playback position
- **BPM Changes**: Playhead speed adjusts to tempo

## 🤖 AI Command Usage

### Basic Commands
- **"재생" / "play"**: Start playback
- **"정지" / "stop"**: Stop playback
- **"120 bpm"**: Set BPM to 120
- **"150 bpm"**: Set BPM to 150

### Command Input
- Enter natural language commands in bottom input field
- Click "실행" / "Execute" button to run commands
- Supports both Korean and English

## 🎛️ Track System Usage

### File Library
- **Add Files**: Click "파일 추가" button in the left library panel
- **Supported Formats**: MP3, WAV, OGG, M4A, AAC
- **File Info**: Duration, sample rate, channels displayed automatically
- **Delete Files**: Use × button on each file item

### Drag & Drop Placement
- **Select File**: Click and drag desired audio file from library
- **Place on Track**: Drop onto desired track at specific time position
- **Time Accuracy**: Files placed precisely at drop location
- **Clip Display**: Audio clips with real-time waveform visualization

### Track Controls
- **Mute**: Use "M" button to mute/unmute each track
- **Solo**: Use "S" button to play only that track
- **Volume**: Slider control for per-track volume (0-100)
- **Remove Clips**: Use × button on clip to delete individually

### Multi-track Editing
- **3 Tracks**: Three tracks provided by default
- **Simultaneous Playback**: Multiple track clips can play together
- **Time Sync**: All tracks synchronized with metronome
- **Waveform Visualization**: Real-time waveform display powered by WaveSurfer.js

## 🎵 Waveform Visualization Features

### Real-time Waveform Display
- **WaveSurfer.js**: Professional-grade waveform rendering engine
- **Logic Pro X Style**: Blue waveforms with professional design
- **High Resolution**: Accurate audio data visualization
- **Transparent Overlay**: Filename and waveform displayed together

## 🔮 Upcoming Features

### Advanced Editing Tools
- Audio clip cut/copy/paste operations
- Fade in/out effects
- Clip movement and resizing

### Mixing Tools
- Pan control (left/right balance)
- Equalizer
- Reverb, delay, and other effects

### AI Feature Expansion
- Automatic rhythm alignment
- Smart mixing suggestions
- Music style analysis
